# Keep the host's build artifacts out of the image.
#
# This is not just a size optimisation -- it is correctness. pnpm's
# per-package `node_modules` contains symlinks with absolute paths into the
# host's store (`C:/Users/.../node_modules/.pnpm/...` on Windows). Copying
# them shadows the symlinks created by the install inside the container, and
# every import then resolves to a path that does not exist, failing at runtime
# with `ERR_MODULE_NOT_FOUND`.
#
# The same applies to `dist` and `*.tsbuildinfo`: a stale host build would
# make `tsc -b` skip work and ship whatever happened to be on the developer's
# disk rather than a clean build.

# Dependencies -- installed inside the image
**/node_modules

# Build output -- compiled inside the image
**/dist
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Rust build output for the desktop client: large, and not used server-side
apps/desktop/src-tauri/target

# Secrets. Configuration is injected at runtime via env_file, never baked in.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.server.example

# Version control and tooling
.git
.gitignore
.github
.vscode
.idea

# Local infrastructure state
.docker-data

# Tests and coverage are not run in the image
coverage
**/*.test.ts
**/*.test.tsx
tests

# Documentation and editor files
docs
*.md
!README.md
.editorconfig
.prettierignore

# Logs
*.log
